Here is the commit message:
fix issues of mrb_gc_unregister introduced in 09b1185

* fixes partial copy of objects in GC root array (due to missing `* sizeof(mrb_value)`)
* restores the behavior that permitted an unregistered object to be used as an argument

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by incorrect handling of the length of the garbage collection root array during the unregistration of objects. Specifically, the code was not properly accounting for the size of the elements being moved in memory, leading to potential memory corruption and incorrect behavior when an unregistered object was used as an argument. The removal of the `len` variable and the adjustment of the memory move operation were necessary to ensure that the correct number of bytes was moved and that the array length was accurately maintained.

Here is the patch:
 /* mrb_gc_unregister() removes the object from GC root. */
 MRB_API void
 mrb_gc_unregister(mrb_state *mrb, mrb_value obj)
 {
   mrb_sym root = mrb_intern_lit(mrb, GC_ROOT_NAME);
   mrb_value table = mrb_gv_get(mrb, root);
   struct RArray *a;
-  mrb_int i, len;
+  mrb_int i;

   if (mrb_nil_p(table)) return;
   if (mrb_type(table) != MRB_TT_ARRAY) {
     mrb_gv_set(mrb, root, mrb_nil_value());
     return;
   }
   a = mrb_ary_ptr(table);
   mrb_ary_modify(mrb, a);
-  len = a->len-1;
-  for (i=0; i<len; i++) {
+  for (i = 0; i < a->len; i++) {
     if (mrb_obj_eq(mrb, a->ptr[i], obj)) {
-      memmove(&a->ptr[i], &a->ptr[i+1], len-i);
+      a->len--;
+      memmove(&a->ptr[i], &a->ptr[i + 1], (a->len - i) * sizeof(a->ptr[i]));
       break;
     }
   }
-  a->len--;
 }



